g speech recognition, natural language understanding, speech signal enhancement, text-to-speech, and acoustic tuning. The company has a strategic partnership with Arm Kleidi; and SiMa.ai to advance the capabilities and performance of CaLLM Edge. Cerence Inc. was incorporated in 2020 and is headquartered in Burlington, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Brian Matthew Krzanich | President, CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $194K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue falling 5%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $36K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $21K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Cerence Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $358M market cap on $252M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -3% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 72% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $47M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 24.2\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 11% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.4% of the shares, and profit capture 